---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="How to Use"
  description="Comprehensive guide on using HabitTrack: 3-state habit cells, reordering rows, reading daily score charts, and offline PWA installation."
>
  <article class="max-w-none">
    <div class="mb-10 text-center sm:text-left border-b border-slate-200 dark:border-purple-900/50 pb-8">
      <span class="inline-block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-indigo-600 dark:text-purple-400 bg-indigo-50 dark:bg-purple-950/60 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-indigo-100 dark:border-purple-800/60 mb-3">
        User Guide
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-50">
        How to Use HabitTrack
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-600 dark:text-purple-200/80 leading-relaxed">
        Everything you need to master your monthly habit tracker in less than 2 minutes.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-12 text-slate-700 dark:text-purple-100/90 leading-relaxed">
      <!-- Step 1 -->
      <section class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 items-start">
        <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-indigo-600 text-white font-bold flex items-center justify-center text-lg shadow-sm">
          1
        </div>
        <div class="flex-1 space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100">
            Adding and Managing Habits
          </h2>
          <p>
            Click the <strong>"+ Add Habit"</strong> button on the header (or floating <strong>+</strong> button on mobile) to create a new routine. You can track as many habits as you want each month.
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm sm:text-base">
            <li><strong>Rename:</strong> Click the three-dot menu (⋮) on any habit row to edit its title.</li>
            <li><strong>Delete:</strong> Remove habits you no longer wish to track from the three-dot menu.</li>
            <li><strong>Reorder:</strong> Grab the drag handle (⠿) on the left side of any row to arrange your habits in your preferred order.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Step 2 -->
      <section class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 items-start">
        <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-indigo-600 text-white font-bold flex items-center justify-center text-lg shadow-sm">
          2
        </div>
        <div class="flex-1 space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100">
            The 3-State Cell Cycle
          </h2>
          <p>
            Each day box operates with a simple, instant tap cycle without opening annoying popups:
          </p>
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 my-4">
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-[#1a0b2e] border border-slate-200 dark:border-purple-800/60 text-center">
              <span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-slate-100 border border-slate-400 dark:bg-[#251340] dark:border-purple-400 text-transparent font-bold mb-2">·</span>
              <h4 class="font-bold text-sm text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100">1. Empty</h4>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-purple-300 mt-1">Default state waiting for input.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-[#1a0b2e] border border-slate-200 dark:border-purple-800/60 text-center">
              <span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-green-500/20 border border-green-500/40 text-green-500 font-bold mb-2">✔</span>
              <h4 class="font-bold text-sm text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100">2. Completed (✔)</h4>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-purple-300 mt-1">Tap once: marked as done (+1 score).</p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-[#1a0b2e] border border-slate-200 dark:border-purple-800/60 text-center">
              <span class="inline-flex items-center justify-center w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-red-500/20 border border-red-500/40 text-red-500 font-bold mb-2">✖</span>
              <h4 class="font-bold text-sm text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100">3. Skipped / Missed (✖)</h4>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 dark:text-purple-300 mt-1">Tap again: intentionally missed (0 score).</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-purple-300">
            A third tap returns the cell back to empty so you can fix mistakes effortlessly.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Step 3 -->
      <section class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 items-start">
        <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-indigo-600 text-white font-bold flex items-center justify-center text-lg shadow-sm">
          3
        </div>
        <div class="flex-1 space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100">
            Score Chart & Completion Rate
          </h2>
          <p>
            Every day your completed habits are automatically aggregated into the <strong>Daily Score Graph</strong>:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm sm:text-base">
            <li><strong>Dynamic Rate:</strong> In the ongoing month, your completion rate is calculated based on days that have already passed (today and prior), ensuring fair metrics.</li>
            <li><strong>Historical Review:</strong> Past months calculate completion rate across the entire month.</li>
            <li><strong>Visual Curve:</strong> Hover or tap any point along the curve to see exact ratio and percentage for that day.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Step 4 -->
      <section class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 items-start">
        <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-indigo-600 text-white font-bold flex items-center justify-center text-lg shadow-sm">
          4
        </div>
        <div class="flex-1 space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100">
            Switching Months
          </h2>
          <p>
            Use the <strong>&lt; Month Year &gt;</strong> selector in the top header to navigate backward or forward. All habits and logs are organized cleanly by month and year.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Step 5 -->
      <section class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-6 items-start">
        <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-indigo-600 text-white font-bold flex items-center justify-center text-lg shadow-sm">
          5
        </div>
        <div class="flex-1 space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-purple-100">
            Installing as a Native App (PWA)
          </h2>
          <p>
            HabitTrack is a Progressive Web App (PWA) that installs on your home screen or desktop:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm sm:text-base">
            <li><strong>iOS (Safari):</strong> Tap the Share button &gt; <em>"Add to Home Screen"</em>.</li>
            <li><strong>Android (Chrome):</strong> Tap the menu (⋮) &gt; <em>"Install app"</em> or <em>"Add to Home Screen"</em>.</li>
            <li><strong>Desktop (Chrome/Edge):</strong> Click the install icon in the address bar to install it as a standalone desktop app.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 text-center">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 bg-indigo-600 hover:bg-indigo-700 dark:bg-purple-600 dark:hover:bg-purple-500 text-white font-semibold px-6 py-3 rounded-xl shadow-sm transition-colors text-sm sm:text-base"
      >
        <span>Open Your Tracker Now</span>
        <span>→</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
